    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-13948",
      "problem": "Find the values of $x$ that satisfy $2x - 5 \\leq 1$ and $7x +11 < -3.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection. \n\n- We start by solving $2x - 5 \\leq 1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5 & \\le 1 \\\\ 2x-5+5 & \\le 1+5 \\\\ 2x & \\le 6 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{2} & \\le \\frac{6}{2} \\\\ x & \\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/600e2c9a8560e61697b480de35a3d077d13624ba616514a060c4bcf4fa3f47e4.png)\n\n- Then, we solve $7x +11 < -3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7x+11 & <-3 \\\\ 7x+11-11 & <-3-11 \\\\ 7x & <-14 \\\\ \\frac{7x}{7} & <\\frac{-14}{7} \\\\ x & <-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/b6014786331de7693c3a1e0d502ea79fb049252fe9f3ecfcd49a873d996896fe.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14194110/assets/2e5425630ece3ab7006378a7930aae0452c3d5261e7bfb579c97daf572b71d22.png)\n\nThus, the final solution is $x < -2.$",
